  "rationale": [
    "Accent = signal blue: the only hue that is not already a safety/status meaning on a shop floor (red stop, green go, yellow caution).",
    "Info merges into the accent (both blue) so the screen has one blue, not two competing ones.",
    "Yellow is a signature, not a status: tape and edges carry it; text on it is always ink (9:1).",
    "Large density and a 1.333 display ratio: read from a metre away with gloves on, big feedback beats subtle hierarchy."
  ],
  "name": "Industrial utility",
  "tags": [
    "industrial",
    "factory",
    "warehouse",
    "operations",
    "counter",
    "logistics",
    "safety",
